# Repository Map Navigation

## Primary navigation source

Before opening any implementation file, read `.cursor/REPO_MAP.md` to locate the correct file.

The map contains: project structure, module responsibilities, entry points, public APIs, shared utilities, dependency relationships, architecture notes, and coding conventions.

## Rules

- Treat `.cursor/REPO_MAP.md` as the authoritative starting point for orientation.
- Open implementation files only after identifying the correct location from the map.
- Update the map incrementally when new modules, patterns, or conventions are discovered — append only, do not rewrite.
- Never rebuild the map from scratch unless explicitly requested.
- Do not read source files "for context" when the map already provides the needed information.
